---
title: IWDG - independent watchdog, nothing to wire
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY. No pins.
%% Clocked by the LSI (~32 kHz), which keeps running even if the main clock
%% or the PLL dies - that is what makes it "independent".
%% Once started it cannot be stopped in software; only a reset clears it.
%% The LSI is untrimmed, so the real timeout can drift by tens of percent.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        LSI["LSI RC ~32 kHz - always available"]
        PRE["Prescaler /4 .. /256"]
        CNT["12-bit down counter"]
        RST["Reset generator"]
        APP["Application main loop"]
        NRST["System reset"]
    end

    LSI --> PRE
    PRE --> CNT
    APP -->|"IWDG_Refresh reloads the counter"| CNT
    CNT -->|"reaches zero"| RST
    RST --> NRST
